## Perspective Verification Details
### 1. Engineering Wing (DE1, DE2, RT)
- DE1 verified HashMap key-value storage with length-prefixed encoding and delimiter isolation, plus JSON parser/serializer with full RFC 8259 error handling.
- DE2 verified CLI project scaffolding (init/new), documentation extraction (doc), monotonic timers under &TimeCap, HTTP client under &NetCap, and SemVer package resolution.
- RT verified C runtime string handling, thread-safe bounded channels under &ThreadCap, WASM .wat execution under wasmtime, and Backend-LLVM SECRET refusal parity.

### 2. Adversarial QA Wing (PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM)
- PV1 executed 9 hostile fuzzing beats covering rapid insert/remove cycles, 5x key overwrites, keys with unicode/spaces/tabs/colons, and unclosed JSON string quotes.
- PV2 proved bounded channel exhaustion (fail-closed full), drain semantics (fail-closed empty), invalid handle rejection, and cross-channel isolation.
- SEC proved default-deny capability gates (compile-time failure on unprivileged effectful calls), deep struct SECRET taint refusal across C and LLVM backends, and Landlock OS sandboxing.
- MEM eliminated stale pointer cache hazards in UTF-8 indexing and verified proper ARC retain/release semantics and RLIMIT_AS heap quotas.

### 3. Integration Wing (INT, HARN, HYG)
- INT confirmed full compiler self-check: oodac check oodac/main.oo passes across all 177 self-hosted modules in ~16.8s / 0.32 GiB RAM.
- HARN confirmed end-to-end native execution of the full test fixture suite.
- HYG confirmed 100% Rule 1.7 compliance (every file <= 256 lines) and clean repository hygiene.

### 4. Command Wing (DOCS, COORD)
- DOCS aligned all task boards, release notes, and documentation with the active pin.
- COORD verified that all 12 perspectives have verified the code without conflicting edits or race conditions.

## Production Readiness Verdict
The openOODA compiler, standard library, runtime, CLI tooling, security sandboxing, and adversarial test suites are verified as PRODUCTION READY for Beta deployment.
